[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"404","stub":{"id":"404","section":"01. MM 69 to Wills Gulch picnic area","altname":"","river":"Lake Creek","difficulty":"Vplus","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"121","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"For a long day put in at the tunnel coming out of the mountain. The cascade of diverted water down to Lake Creek proper is fun.","id":"726","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"put in","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This is a very dangerous seive, and is reported to be a mandatory portage. Make sure to scout the location of this rapid just above the South Fork of Lake Creek Road. Or, put-in right below the seive and catch a mile or so of fun warm-up IV before it mellows out again.","id":"727","location":{"latitude":"39.06809997558594","longitude":"-106.50800323486328"},"name":"Tombstone Rapid","distance":"2.2","photoID":"0","difficulty":"VI","approximate":true},{"type":"access","description":"The Road 82c bridge provides access to the creek below Tombstone Rapid.","id":"102014","location":{"latitude":"39.06712341308594","longitude":"-106.50541687011719"},"name":"Road 82c, SF Lake Creek Rd","distance":"2.38","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"Not In My Back Yard, there are several summer homes surrounding this beautiful rapid so you can't scout it until you boat down to the entrance. At the top of the rapid there is a park bench with a no tresspassing sign next to it. Despite the sign it is OK to scout on river right, just be low profile and respectfull. The [entrance drop](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2226) has logs stretched across it at head level, the middle is a fast s-turn with [undercuts](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2229) leading into a [constriction](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2227). Then the creek splits, river right is a waterfall and [left](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2228) is a smaller broken fall.","id":"728","location":{"latitude":"39.071067810058594","longitude":"-106.46790313720703"},"name":"NIMBY Rapid","distance":"4","photoID":"2226","difficulty":"V+","approximate":true},{"type":"access","description":"This is would be a relatively simple 10' [waterfall](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2230) if it weren't for the fact that it pours directly into a huge undercut boulder. A hard boof left will just barely land you away from the undercut. This rapid is one of the main reasons I call Lake Creek schizophrenic, there is nothing but boring Class II a mile above and below it. Take out just downstream if you don't want to run the Lower Gorge.","id":"729","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Toaster Rapid","distance":"6","photoID":"2230","difficulty":"V","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"This is a very technical waterfall. The hardest part is negotiating a tricky seam just a few feet above the lip of the falls. After The Brain you are stuck in a steep little gorge, getting out to scout or portage Paralyzer Rapid(VI) is difficult.","id":"730","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"The Brain Rapid","distance":"7.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"V+","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"Whether you consider this a V+ or VI, one fact is undisputed: this cascade is huge!","id":"731","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Paralyzer Rapid","distance":"8","photoID":"1006","difficulty":"V+","approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"This rapid could almost be considered the run out of Paralyzer, but there is a small pool between them. Z-turn looks insignificant compared to Paralyzer but it's actually much more dangerous. The current makes a severe left turn and slams directly into a badly undercut cliff. The trick is to boof right over the guard rock pushing the current left. The move is scariest at low flows and gets easier with more water.","id":"732","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Z-turn Rapid","distance":"8.1","photoID":null,"difficulty":"V+","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This bridge provides a take out above the lower Gorge.","id":"734","location":{"latitude":"39.06733703613281","longitude":"-106.41079711914062"},"name":"Parry Creek Campground Bridge","distance":"8.3","photoID":"0","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"This is one of the best rapids in Colorado! It's a pounding funneling waterfall that dumps you in a big bubbling rock cauldron! At low flows the narrow exit from the cauldron is blocked by wood.","id":"733","location":{"latitude":"39.06251525878906","longitude":"-106.40670013427734"},"name":"Cauldron Rapid","distance":"8.7","photoID":"0","difficulty":"V+","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"1006","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3120","description":"","caption":"Paralyzer","poi_name":"Paralyzer","subject":"Gordon Dalton","author":"Wendy Knick","poi_id":"734","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1006","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1006"}},{"id":"6876","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3183","description":"","caption":"Paralyzed","poi_name":"Paralyzer","subject":"?","author":"Jered Johnson","poi_id":"731","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6876","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6876"}},{"id":"2227","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3184","description":"","caption":"Middle NIMBY","poi_name":"N.I.M.B.Y.","subject":"Brian Adkins","author":"Matt Stiegler","poi_id":"727","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2227","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2227"}},{"id":"2226","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3184","description":"","caption":"Upper NIMBY","poi_name":"N.I.M.B.Y.","subject":"","author":"Matt Stiegler","poi_id":"727","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2226","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2226"}},{"id":"2229","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3184","description":"This is a tricky little rock outcropping just below the crux of NIMBY that is rather hard to avoid.","caption":"Tricky rock outcropping","poi_name":"N.I.M.B.Y.","subject":"Matt Stiegler","author":"Matt Stiegler","poi_id":"727","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2229","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2229"}},{"id":"2230","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3184","description":"Boof LEFT!!!","caption":"Toaster Falls","poi_name":"Toaster","subject":"Brian Adkins","author":"Matt Stiegler","poi_id":"733","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2230","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2230"}},{"id":"2228","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3184","description":"On the bottom half of NIMBY the creek splits in two, this is the river left channel.  The river right channel is a waterfall.","caption":"Lower NIMBY","poi_name":"N.I.M.B.Y.","subject":"Matt Stiegler","author":"Matt Stiegler","poi_id":"727","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2228","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2228"}},{"id":"886817","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889573","description":"Runnable but low","caption":"Cauldron","poi_name":"Cauldron","subject":"","author":"Kaelan Hendrickson","poi_id":"729","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886817","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886817"}}],"detail":{"id":"404","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Lake Creek is a schizophrenic stream. 1/2 of it is meandering Class II, 1/3 is undefined continuous Class IV, and the rest is a handfull of **sick** V+ bedrock gorges. If you run the upper half be sure you scout the locations of Tombstone(V) and Toaster(V) before putting on.  Floating into either could be fatal if you have not scouted them and don't realize what they are. If you run the Lower Gorge(V+,VI), make sure to scout the whole thing! Last but not least, do not forget to run Cauldron Rapid(V)! It's the second biggest drop, but lacks some of the scare factors of the rapids upstream.\n\nThe entire run parallels Hwy 82. The upper put-in is at milemarker 69, the take-out above the Lower Gorge is at mm 74.5, and Cauldron Rapid is at about mm 79.\n\nIn 2003 Lake Creek ran at huge levels (almost 2000cfs) for almost an entire month, as a result I have heard that almost all rapids had changed, some dramatic - some minor. Most significant was Tombstone which turned into an unrunnable sieve, no ifs and or butts this is now a mandatory portage!!!","averageGradient":"137","maxGradient":"235","length":"9.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"404","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"300","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"LAKE CREEK ABOVE TWIN LAKES RESERVOIR, CO.","gaugeSource":"COLORADO_DEPARTMENT_OF_WATER_RESOURCES","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"LAKATLCO","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"121","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":null,"location":{"latitude":"39.063019","longitude":"-106.407634"},"externalSourceLinks":null},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nLow Runnable Range (R0-R5): 300 - 500 cfs  Comment: Best range for the hard rapids.\nHigh Runnable Range (R5-R9): 500 - 1000 cfs  Comment: Best range for the easier sections. Portage the hard rapids.\n\nMigration Errors: \nFor two ranges, R0 to R9 is not covered exactly","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"121","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["726","727","102014","728","729","730","731","732","734","733"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-106.54099478673402,39.08193794767038],[-106.54066761069288,39.08194270704536],[-106.54039873152664,39.08193794767038],[-106.54018398465195,39.081923076837086],[-106.539934141944,39.081904041420444],[-106.53973188777769,39.081946870587046],[-106.53968461173605,39.08208580600348],[-106.53960007840288,39.08201440600362],[-106.53956487840293,39.08198140600365],[-106.5395930784029,39.081926472670375],[-106.53965647840278,39.08181660600388],[-106.5396636117361,39.081717806004065],[-106.5395368117363,39.081591406004236],[-106.5393536117366,39.08154740600435],[-106.53918447840353,39.081470606004416],[-106.53900127840382,39.08131120600467],[-106.5386208117377,39.08099820600518],[-106.53848007840463,39.08085527267207],[-106.53839541173807,39.08070707267228],[-106.53836741173814,39.08059160600578],[-106.53834627840479,39.08048180600599],[-106.53826181173827,39.08032247267289],[-106.53800821173866,39.08006440600661],[-106.53784607840561,39.079899606006904],[-106.53768407840585,39.07980620600705],[-106.53752907840607,39.079800672673684],[-106.53732467840638,39.079811672673664],[-106.53708521174013,39.07985000600695],[-106.53688781174